{%- comment -%}
  zv-woning-variants (2026-10-27): prints the variant id of each Woning product (one for the
  NAMI packages, one for the Climax packages; surcharges[] in pricing.config.json), pipe-separated
  and in the same order as `handles`, so entry i is the product whose packages are entry i of
  zv_woning_applies_by_product (and woning.products[i] in #zv-pricing-config).

  A product resolves only if it exists and its first variant's SKU is the config's, the same check
  as for the packages by handle. One that doesn't prints 0: that keeps the list parallel (a blank
  entry at the end would be dropped by split) and never matches a cart line. Its packages then fall
  back to the Woning property alone, without a priced line.

  Params (render scope can't see the caller's zv_* variables, so pass them in):
    handles - zv_woning_handles, or the output of zv-package-handles, line: 'woning'
    skus    - zv_woning_skus, or zv-package-handles, line: 'woning', what: 'skus'
  Usage: capture it, then `| strip`, and `| split: '|'` for a list of strings.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign wv_handles = handles | split: '|'
  assign wv_skus = skus | split: '|'
  assign wv_out = ''
  for h in wv_handles
    assign wv_id = 0
    assign wv_p = all_products[h]
    if h != blank and wv_p != blank and wv_p.id != blank and wv_p.variants.first.sku == wv_skus[forloop.index0]
      assign wv_id = wv_p.variants.first.id
    endif
    if forloop.first
      assign wv_out = wv_id | append: ''
    else
      assign wv_out = wv_out | append: '|' | append: wv_id
    endif
  endfor
  echo wv_out
-%}
